> Comment placement matrix for the ns form.
>
> Every case is one cell of: section x comment position x comment kind x whether the
> section is the last main form in the input. The comment is either a line comment
> (;; c1) or a discard form (#_ :c1). Each case must format correctly, be idempotent,
> and keep the comment exactly once in the output.
>
> Cells affected by an open bug are not in this file yet; they are listed in the issue
> for that bug and should be added here once it is fixed.
>
> The rule being tested: a comment or discard form attaches to the nearest item to its
> left on the same line and travels with that item when the item is sorted. Closing
> parens are not items, so a comment after [a.b])) belongs to a.b. If nothing is to its
> left on that line, it is a comment above the next item.

# ns comment matrix: comment above - refer-clojure - comment - last main form

--Input
(ns foo
  ;; c1
  (:refer-clojure :exclude [get assoc]))

(def x 1)
--Input

--Expected
(ns foo
  ;; c1
  (:refer-clojure :exclude [assoc get]))

(def x 1)
--Expected

# ns comment matrix: comment above - refer-clojure - comment - not last main form

--Input
(ns foo
  ;; c1
  (:refer-clojure :exclude [get assoc])
  (:require [z.z]))

(def x 1)
--Input

--Expected
(ns foo
  ;; c1
  (:refer-clojure :exclude [assoc get])
  (:require
   [z.z]))

(def x 1)
--Expected

# ns comment matrix: comment above - refer-clojure - discard - last main form

--Input
(ns foo
  #_ :c1
  (:refer-clojure :exclude [get assoc]))

(def x 1)
--Input

--Expected
(ns foo
  #_ :c1
  (:refer-clojure :exclude [assoc get]))

(def x 1)
--Expected

